/// One promotional banner strip on the homepage — a merchant-created, named,
/// ordered row of promo tiles with its own layout.
///
/// The storefront used to render exactly one three-across promo strip: one
/// `MID_BANNERS` key in the section registry, one `MID` value in
/// BannerPlacement, and `sm:grid-cols-3` hardcoded into MidBanners.tsx. A
/// merchant who wanted a single full-width promo, or two half-width ones, or a
/// second strip further down the page, had none of those. A group is that
/// strip made into data: the COUNT of strips is now merchant data rather than
/// a compiled-in tuple.
///
/// ── Why a table, and not a JSON array on StoreSetting ────────────────────
///
/// Banner membership is a relation. A banner id inside a JSON array has no
/// foreign key, so deleting a banner would leave a dangling id that every
/// reader has to defend against forever — and this repo's own rule is that a
/// Json column is unconstrained by Postgres, leaving the Zod schema as the only
/// gate. A real column with `onDelete: SetNull` makes the detach behaviour the
/// database's job rather than seven call sites'.
///
/// ── DELETING A GROUP DETACHES ITS BANNERS, IT DOES NOT DELETE THEM ───────
///
/// `Banner.promoBannerGroup` is declared `onDelete: SetNull`, so removing a
/// group leaves every banner it held on file with no group. A merchant who
/// deletes a strip is removing an ARRANGEMENT, not throwing away artwork they
/// paid someone to make. Detached banners surface in the admin's banner list as
/// unassigned, which is a state the merchant can already see and fix by
/// assigning them elsewhere. Do not change this to Cascade.
///
/// Deleting a group also drops the homepage section entry naming it — not by a
/// write here, but because `reconcileHomeConfig` discards an entry whose group
/// no longer exists. That is the same path an unregistered section key already
/// takes: there is no component left that could render it.
///
/// See openspec/changes/add-promo-banner-groups, design.md Decisions 1 and 2.
model PromoBannerGroup {
  id String @id @default(uuid(7))

  /// The merchant's own label for the strip — "Week deals", "iPhone push".
  /// Shown in the admin's Home Sections list so a merchant with three strips
  /// can tell which row is which; the storefront does NOT render it. A
  /// group-level heading above the strip is deliberately out of scope, see the
  /// change's design.md Open Questions.
  name String

  /// How many tiles the strip renders across. Resolved on read rather than
  /// trusted — an unrecognised value reads back as THREE — mirroring
  /// `resolveSectionVariant`'s handling of a layout from a newer server.
  ///
  /// Lives HERE and not on the homeConfig entry because it is a property of
  /// this strip, and a strip's identity is the group. On the config entry, the
  /// same group would render at different widths depending on which entry
  /// named it, and "delete the entry, re-add it" would silently lose the
  /// layout.
  layout PromoBannerLayout @default(THREE)

  /// The merchant's ordering among groups, ascending. This orders the groups
  /// themselves — where each STRIP sits on the page is the homepage section
  /// configuration's business, not this column's. It decides only the position
  /// a newly-created group is spliced into that configuration at, and the order
  /// the admin's manager lists them in.
  sortOrder Int @default(0)

  banners Banner[]

  createdAt DateTime @default(now())
  updatedAt DateTime @updatedAt

  @@index([sortOrder])
}
